<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ domain.TITLE }} · {{ facts.summary("period_label") }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="{{ domain.DESCRIPTION }}">
<style>
:root {
  --ink: #0b0b0b;
  --body: #2b2926;
  --muted: #6f6d6a;
  --soft: #9a9793;
  --hair: #e8e5e1;
  --hair-strong: #d8d4cf;
  --canvas: #f6f5f3;
  --card: #ffffff;
  --blue: #2563eb;
  --coral: #d95f4b;
  --green: #15803d;
  --radius: 18px;
  --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, "Book Antiqua", Georgia, serif;
  --sans: Inter, "InterVariable", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  --mono: "SF Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { color-scheme: light; }
body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--canvas);
  color: var(--ink);
  font: 15px/1.55 var(--sans);
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
}
.glow {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0 0 auto 0;
  height: 780px;
  pointer-events: none;
  background:
    radial-gradient(52% 70% at 18% 2%, rgba(255, 190, 180, .48), transparent 62%),
    radial-gradient(46% 65% at 52% 0%, rgba(198, 183, 255, .36), transparent 66%),
    radial-gradient(50% 70% at 86% 2%, rgba(166, 210, 255, .42), transparent 62%);
  filter: blur(28px);
  opacity: .9;
  z-index: 0;
}
.page {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
  max-width: 1120px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 30px 36px 76px;
}
.masthead { padding: 26px 0 0; }
.topline {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 16px;
  padding-bottom: 44px;
}
.brand {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 9px;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 12.5px;
  letter-spacing: -.01em;
}
.mark { width: 15px; height: 15px; fill: currentColor; flex: none; }
.pill {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 7px;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 5px 10px 5px 9px;
  border: 1px solid var(--hair);
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .62);
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 11.5px;
  line-height: 1;
  backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
}
.pill .dot {
  width: 5px;
  height: 5px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--coral);
  flex: none;
}
h1, h2, h3 { margin: 0; }
h1 {
  max-width: 940px;
  font-size: clamp(44px, 7.2vw, 76px);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: .96;
  letter-spacing: -.052em;
}
.standfirst {
  max-width: 620px;
  margin: 24px 0 0;
  color: #45423e;
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: 21px;
  line-height: 1.45;
  letter-spacing: -.005em;
}
.meta {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 20px;
  margin: 40px 0 0;
  padding: 16px 0 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-strong);
}
.meta dt {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--soft);
  font-size: 10.5px;
  letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.meta dd {
  margin: 4px 0 0;
  color: var(--body);
  font-size: 13px;
  letter-spacing: -.01em;
}
.notice {
  margin: 26px 0 0;
  padding: 15px 17px;
  border: 1px solid #f0d7cf;
  border-radius: 14px;
  background: #fffaf8;
  color: #7c2d1e;
  font-size: 13.5px;
}
.notice strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; font-weight: 600; }
.notice ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 17px; }
.notice code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; }
.cards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 14px;
  margin: 40px 0 0;
}
.card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: space-between;
  min-height: 168px;
  padding: 18px 18px 16px;
  border: 1px solid var(--hair);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  background: var(--card);
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(10, 10, 10, .03);
}
.card.accent {
  border-color: #f1d7cf;
  background: linear-gradient(158deg, #ffffff 30%, #fff5f2 100%);
}
.card .value {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 43px;
  font-weight: 550;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: -.05em;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.card.accent .value { color: var(--coral); }
.card .value .of { color: var(--soft); font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
.card .label {
  margin: 12px 0 0;
  color: var(--body);
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: 500;
  line-height: 1.35;
}
.card .note { margin: 3px 0 0; color: var(--soft); font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.4; }
section { margin-top: 76px; }
.kicker {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  color: var(--soft);
  font-size: 10.5px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: .09em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.kicker::before {
  content: "";
  width: 4px;
  height: 4px;
  border-radius: 1px;
  background: var(--ink);
  flex: none;
}
h2 {
  font-size: 34px;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.14;
  letter-spacing: -.035em;
}
.lede {
  max-width: 62ch;
  margin: 12px 0 0;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.55;
}
.prose { max-width: 760px; }
.prose p { margin: 0 0 17px; color: var(--body); font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.68; }
.prose p:first-of-type {
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: #383531;
}
.prose p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.prose strong { font-weight: 600; }
.panel {
  margin-top: 26px;
  padding: 22px 22px 18px;
  border: 1px solid var(--hair);
  border-radius: var(--radius);
  background: var(--card);
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(10, 10, 10, .03);
}
figure { margin: 14px 0 0; }
figure svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
figcaption {
  margin: 14px 2px 2px;
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 12.5px;
  line-height: 1.55;
}
figcaption strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 550; }
.statline {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 10px;
  margin: 26px 0 0;
  padding-top: 16px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  color: var(--muted);
  font-size: 13px;
}
.statline strong { color: var(--coral); font-size: 30px; font-weight: 550; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
th {
  padding: 7px 8px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair-strong);
  color: var(--soft);
  font-size: 10px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-align: left;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
td { padding: 9px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); vertical-align: top; }
tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.badge {
  display: inline-block;
  padding: 2px 8px;
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-size: 10.5px;
  font-weight: 500;
  line-height: 1.3;
}
.badge.differs { background: #fdeee9; color: #a33a27; }
.badge.match { background: #eaf5ee; color: #1f6b3a; }
.badge.missing { background: #fde8e6; color: #9f1f1a; }
.hash, code, .path { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11.5px; }
.hash, .path { color: var(--soft); }
.table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
.table-wrap table { min-width: 560px; }
details { margin-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); padding-top: 14px; }
summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; }
summary:hover { color: var(--ink); }
details table { margin-top: 12px; }
.stages {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 24px;
  margin: 30px 0 0;
  padding: 20px 0 0;
  list-style: none;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-strong);
}
.stages li { position: relative; min-width: 0; }
.stages li::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: -23px;
  left: 0;
  width: 5px;
  height: 5px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--ink);
}
.stages .n {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  color: var(--soft);
  font-size: 10.5px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: .08em;
}
.stages h3 { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 550; letter-spacing: -.005em; }
.stages p { margin: 6px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; }
.versions { margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--soft); font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.7; }
.versions code { color: var(--muted); }
footer { margin-top: 84px; }
.ghost {
  margin: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
  color: rgba(11, 11, 11, .055);
  font-size: clamp(64px, 15vw, 178px);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: .78;
  letter-spacing: -.065em;
  white-space: nowrap;
  user-select: none;
}
.colophon {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 18px;
  margin-top: 26px;
  padding-top: 16px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--hair-strong);
  color: var(--soft);
  font-size: 11.5px;
  line-height: 1.6;
}
.colophon p { max-width: 560px; margin: 0; }
.colophon strong { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 550; }
.visually-hidden {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
  white-space: nowrap;
}
@media (max-width: 980px) {
  .page { padding: 24px 22px 56px; }
  .topline { padding-bottom: 34px; }
  .cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}
@media (max-width: 820px) {
  .stages {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
  .stages li { padding: 14px 0 14px 18px; border-left: 1px solid var(--hair-strong); }
  .stages li::before { top: 20px; left: -3px; }
  .stages .n { margin-bottom: 6px; }
}
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .table-wrap { overflow: visible; }
  .table-wrap table { min-width: 0; }
  .table-wrap thead { display: none; }
  .table-wrap tbody { display: block; }
  .table-wrap tr {
    display: block;
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .table-wrap tr:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .table-wrap td {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 3px 0;
    border: 0;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .table-wrap td::before {
    content: attr(data-label);
    flex: none;
    color: var(--soft);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: .07em;
    text-align: left;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .table-wrap td:first-child { font-weight: 550; }
  .table-wrap td code { word-break: break-all; }
}
@media (max-width: 620px) {
  .page { padding: 18px 18px 44px; }
  h1 { font-size: 40px; }
  .standfirst { font-size: 18px; }
  .meta { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 14px; }
  .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .card { min-height: 132px; }
  section { margin-top: 56px; }
  .panel { padding: 16px 14px 14px; border-radius: 15px; }
  h2 { font-size: 28px; }
  .prose p:first-of-type { font-size: 19px; }
  figure svg text { font-size: 16.5px; }
  .ghost { font-size: 13vw; }
}
@media print {
  body { background: #fff; }
  .glow, .ghost { display: none; }
  .page { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
  .panel, .card, .stages li { box-shadow: none; }
  h2 { break-after: avoid; }
  figure, table, .card, .stages li { break-inside: avoid; }
  details { display: none; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<main class="page">

  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="topline">
      <p class="brand">
        <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="4" height="4"/><rect x="8" y="0" width="4" height="4"/>
          <rect x="4" y="4" width="4" height="4"/><rect x="12" y="4" width="4" height="4"/>
          <rect x="0" y="8" width="4" height="4"/><rect x="8" y="8" width="4" height="4"/>
          <rect x="4" y="12" width="4" height="4"/>
        </svg>
        {{ domain.SUBTITLE }}
      </p>
      <p class="pill"><span class="dot"></span> Fixture data</p>
    </div>
    <h1>{{ domain.TITLE }}</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">{{ domain.DESCRIPTION }}</p>
    <dl class="meta">
      <div><dt>Period</dt><dd>{{ facts.summary("period_label") }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Measurements</dt><dd>{{ facts.summary("counts.readings") | n0 }} hourly</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Stations</dt><dd>{{ facts.summary("counts.stations") }} reference sites</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Data date</dt><dd>{{ facts.summary("as_of") | date_label }}</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  {% if failed_checks %}
  <aside class="notice">
    <strong>{{ failed_checks | length }} check{% if failed_checks | length != 1 %}s{% endif %} did not pass.</strong>
    <ul>
      {% for check in failed_checks %}
      <li><code>{{ check.name }}</code>: {{ check.detail }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </aside>
  {% endif %}

  {% set pm25 = domain.POLLUTANTS_BY_ID["PM2.5"] %}
  {% set no2 = domain.POLLUTANTS_BY_ID["NO2"] %}
  {% set worst = facts.extreme("annual_station", "mean_value", mode="max", pollutant="PM2.5") %}
  {% set best = facts.extreme("annual_station", "mean_value", mode="min", pollutant="PM2.5") %}
  {% set worst_no2 = facts.extreme("annual_station", "mean_value", mode="max", pollutant="NO2") %}
  {% set differing = facts.rows("claims_checked") | selectattr("verdict", "equalto", "differs") | list %}

  <section class="cards" aria-label="At a glance">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="value">{{ facts.summary("counts.pm25_station_days_over") }}</p>
      <div>
        <p class="label">PM2.5 station-days over the 24-hour limit</p>
        <p class="note">daily mean above {{ pm25.short_term_objective | n0 }} µg/m³</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="value">{{ worst.mean_value | n1 }}</p>
      <div>
        <p class="label">Highest annual PM2.5 mean</p>
        <p class="note">{{ worst.station_name }}, µg/m³</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="value">{{ worst_no2.mean_value | n1 }}</p>
      <div>
        <p class="label">Highest annual NO2 mean</p>
        <p class="note">{{ worst_no2.station_name }}, µg/m³</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="card{% if differing %} accent{% endif %}">
      <p class="value">{{ facts.summary("counts.claims_differ") }}<span class="of">/{{ facts.summary("counts.claims") }}</span></p>
      <div>
        <p class="label">Published figures differ</p>
        <p class="note">by more than {{ domain.CLAIM_TOLERANCE }} µg/m³</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section id="summary">
    <p class="kicker">01 — Summary</p>
    <h2>What the data shows</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The network recorded {{ facts.summary("counts.readings") | n0 }} hourly measurements between
        {{ facts.summary("period.start") | date_label }} and {{ facts.summary("period.end") | date_label }},
        with every station and pollutant at {{ facts.summary("headlines.coverage_min") | pct }} coverage or better.
      </p>
      <p>
        {{ worst.station_name }} recorded the highest annual PM2.5 mean,
        <strong>{{ worst.mean_value | n1 }} µg/m³</strong>,
        {% if worst.mean_value > pm25.annual_objective %}
        {{ (worst.mean_value - pm25.annual_objective) | n1 }} µg/m³ above
        {% else %}
        {{ (pm25.annual_objective - worst.mean_value) | n1 }} µg/m³ below
        {% endif %}
        the {{ pm25.annual_objective | n0 }} µg/m³ objective. {{ best.station_name }} was lowest at
        {{ best.mean_value | n1 }} µg/m³. PM2.5 crossed the {{ pm25.short_term_objective | n0 }} µg/m³
        {{ pm25.short_term_period }} on <strong>{{ facts.summary("counts.pm25_station_days_over") }}</strong>
        station-days, concentrated in the winter months.
      </p>
      <p>
        NO2 peaked at {{ worst_no2.mean_value | n1 }} µg/m³ at {{ worst_no2.station_name }},
        below its {{ no2.annual_objective | n0 }} µg/m³ annual objective.
        {% if facts.summary("counts.no2_station_days_over") %}
        It exceeded the {{ no2.short_term_objective | n0 }} µg/m³ {{ no2.short_term_period }} on
        {{ facts.summary("counts.no2_station_days_over") }} station-days.
        {% else %}
        It did not breach the {{ no2.short_term_objective | n0 }} µg/m³ {{ no2.short_term_period }} at any station.
        {% endif %}
      </p>
      <p>
        {% if differing %}
        Of the {{ facts.summary("counts.claims") }} monthly means the network published,
        <strong>{{ differing | length }} differ</strong> from the measurements by more than
        {{ domain.CLAIM_TOLERANCE }} µg/m³. Each is listed below with the line it came from.
        {% else %}
        Every one of the {{ facts.summary("counts.claims") }} monthly means the network published
        matches the measurements within {{ domain.CLAIM_TOLERANCE }} µg/m³.
        {% endif %}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="figures">
    <p class="kicker">02 — Figures</p>
    <h2>Four views of the year</h2>
    <div class="panel">
      <figure>
        {{ charts.pm25_monthly | safe }}
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 1.</strong> Monthly mean PM2.5 at each station. Winter episodes lift all three stations together; the coastal station is consistently lowest.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <figure>
        {{ charts.pm25_annual | safe }}
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 2.</strong> Annual mean PM2.5 against the {{ pm25.annual_objective | n0 }} µg/m³ objective. The dashed line is the objective, not a measurement.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <figure>
        {{ charts.no2_annual | safe }}
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 3.</strong> Annual mean NO2 against the {{ no2.annual_objective | n0 }} µg/m³ objective. NO2 is usually the harder limit to meet; this network stays below it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <figure>
        {{ charts.pm25_days | safe }}
        <figcaption><strong>Figure 4.</strong> Station-days above the {{ pm25.short_term_objective | n0 }} µg/m³ 24-hour objective, summed across the three stations. A station-day counts each station once per day.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="reconciliation">
    <p class="kicker">03 — Reconciliation</p>
    <h2>Published figures, checked</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Each note states a monthly mean for every station and pollutant. The lakehouse extracts
      those figures with their line, joins them to the measured monthly mean, and reports the
      difference. A figure with no measurement is a failure, not a match.
    </p>
    {% if differing %}
    <p class="statline"><strong>{{ differing | length }}</strong> of {{ facts.summary("counts.claims") }} published figures differ</p>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="panel">
        {% if differing %}
        <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Published figures that differ from the measurements</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Month</th>
              <th>Station</th>
              <th>Pollutant</th>
              <th class="num">Published</th>
              <th class="num">Measured</th>
              <th class="num">Difference</th>
              <th>Source</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {% for claim in differing %}
            <tr>
              <td data-label="Month">{{ claim.month | month_label }}</td>
              <td data-label="Station">{{ claim.station_id | capitalize }}</td>
              <td data-label="Pollutant">{{ claim.pollutant }}</td>
              <td class="num" data-label="Published">{{ claim.published_value | n1 }}</td>
              <td class="num" data-label="Measured">{{ claim.measured_value | n2 }}</td>
              <td class="num" data-label="Difference">{{ "%+.2f" | format(claim.difference) }}</td>
              <td data-label="Source"><code>{{ claim.source_path }}:{{ claim.line }}</code></td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        </div>
        {% endif %}

        <details>
          <summary>Show all {{ facts.summary("counts.claims") }} checked figures</summary>
          <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Month</th>
                <th>Station</th>
                <th>Pollutant</th>
                <th class="num">Published</th>
                <th class="num">Measured</th>
                <th class="num">Difference</th>
                <th>Verdict</th>
                <th>Source</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for claim in facts.rows("claims_checked") %}
              <tr>
                <td data-label="Month">{{ claim.month | month_label }}</td>
                <td data-label="Station">{{ claim.station_id | capitalize }}</td>
                <td data-label="Pollutant">{{ claim.pollutant }}</td>
                <td class="num" data-label="Published">{{ claim.published_value | n1 }}</td>
                <td class="num" data-label="Measured">{% if claim.measured_value is not none %}{{ claim.measured_value | n2 }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
                <td class="num" data-label="Difference">{% if claim.difference is not none %}{{ "%+.2f" | format(claim.difference) }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
                <td data-label="Verdict"><span class="badge {{ claim.verdict }}">{{ claim.verdict }}</span></td>
                <td data-label="Source"><code>{{ claim.source_path }}:{{ claim.line }}</code></td>
              </tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          </div>
        </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="method">
    <p class="kicker">04 — Method</p>
    <h2>How this was built</h2>
    <ol class="stages">
      <li>
        <span class="n">01</span>
        <h3>Source</h3>
        <p>{{ facts.summary("counts.readings") | n0 }} hourly readings and {{ facts.summary("counts.months") }} published notes, from one deterministic pull.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">02</span>
        <h3>Evidence</h3>
        <p>Every reading validated against its contract, then daily and monthly means in dbt: {{ provenance.tables.monthly_station }} monthly rows, {{ provenance.tables.station_coverage }} coverage rows.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">03</span>
        <h3>Insight</h3>
        <p>{{ provenance.tables.claims_checked }} published figures extracted with their note and line, then joined to the measurement they describe.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">04</span>
        <h3>Analysis</h3>
        <p>Five tables, four charts, and {{ facts.checks() | length }} checks. The report's numbers are lookups from those tables, never re-typed prose.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">05</span>
        <h3>Report</h3>
        <p>This page. It is self-contained, opens offline, and is rebuilt byte-for-byte from the same pull.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="provenance">
    <p class="kicker">05 — Provenance</p>
    <h2>What this was built from</h2>
    <p class="lede">Every input is pinned by hash. These are the exact bytes this report was built from.</p>
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Input</th><th class="num">Bytes</th><th>SHA-256</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for item in provenance.inputs %}
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Input">{{ item.label }}<br><span class="path">{{ item.path }}</span></td>
            <td class="num" data-label="Bytes">{{ item.bytes | n0 }}</td>
            <td data-label="SHA-256"><span class="hash">{{ item.sha256[:16] }}…</span></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
      <p class="versions">
        Data date {{ facts.summary("as_of") | date_label }}. Built from
        {% if provenance.git.commit %}{{ provenance.git.branch }} at {{ provenance.git.commit[:12] }}{% if provenance.git.dirty %} with uncommitted changes{% endif %}{% else %}a checkout with no git metadata{% endif %}.
        Python {{ provenance.python }}.
      </p>
      <p class="versions">
        {% for name, version in provenance.packages.items() %}{{ name }} {{ version or "not installed" }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p class="ghost" aria-hidden="true">source → report</p>
    <div class="colophon">
      <p><strong>Fixture data.</strong> The measurements and notes on this page are synthetic and deterministic; they are not a real monitoring network.</p>
      <p>Reference preset for Phlo. To adapt it, replace the domain pack: <code>src/source_to_report/domain</code>, <code>workflows</code> and <code>data</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
